# The golden cases `make eval` runs through the chassis, in the platform's golden-set schema
# (eval_kit.golden; a copy is agent_testkit.evalcases.CASES_SCHEMA). Each case: `id` (g01, g02,
# ...), `task`, `input` ("simplify: ...", sent as the run's `{"text": ...}`), `expect`
# (`contains`, optional `banned`, `tool_calls: []`), `rubric` (what the judge checks), `reference`
# (a model answer), and `label` (the human label of `reference`). Use `task: simplifier` only: the
# schema's other task, `lookup`, must expect a tool call, and this eval does not script tool calls
# yet, so a lookup case stops `make eval` with an error.
#
# Offline, the fake model is scripted per case: it answers each case's input with its reference.
# The scripted judge passes an answer that holds a reference labeled `pass` and fails any other,
# with a score (1 or 0) in reports/eval.json. So a `pass` case checks that your logic keeps the
# model's answer whole. Add cases on what your logic adds. A run that ends in a status other than
# ok or fallback fails its case.
version: 1
cases:
  - id: g01
    task: simplifier
    input: "simplify: hello big world"
    expect:
      contains: [hello, world]
      tool_calls: []
    rubric: The answer keeps every fact of the input in plain words.
    reference: Hello, big world.
    label: pass
